<file path="docs/tests/edge-gradients.html">
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Gradient Contrast Edge Cases</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; margin: 0; padding: 32px; background: #f8f8f8; }
    h1 { font-size: 24px; margin-bottom: 24px; }
    .test-card { padding: 24px; margin-bottom: 16px; border-radius: 8px; }
    .label { font-size: 12px; color: #666; margin-bottom: 4px; }
    .expect { font-size: 11px; color: #888; margin-top: 8px; }

    /* Test 1: Multiple linear gradients (white overlay on colored gradient) - SHOULD PASS */
    .test-multi-gradient {
      background: linear-gradient(rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85)),
                  linear-gradient(135deg, hsla(19, 57%, 47%, 0.35) 0%, hsla(232, 24%, 24%, 0.12) 100%);
      color: #000;
    }

    /* Test 2: Radial gradient dot pattern + solid bg - SHOULD PASS */
    .test-radial-dot {
      background-color: #f5f0eb;
      background-image: radial-gradient(circle, hsla(19, 50%, 55%, 0.25) 1px, transparent 1px);
      background-size: 16px 16px;
      color: #1a1a1a;
    }

    /* Test 3: Dark gradient with light text - SHOULD PASS */
    .test-dark-gradient {
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1e293b 0%, #334155 100%);
      color: #f1f5f9;
    }

    /* Test 4: Low contrast gradient - SHOULD FAIL */
    .test-low-contrast {
      background: linear-gradient(to right, #e5e7eb, #d1d5db);
      color: #9ca3af;
    }

    /* Test 5: Semi-transparent overlay on white - SHOULD PASS (high contrast) */
    .test-semi-transparent {
      background: linear-gradient(rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05), rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05));
      color: #111827;
    }

    /* Test 6: Multiple gradient layers with semi-transparency - SHOULD PASS */
    .test-triple-layer {
      background: linear-gradient(rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9)),
                  linear-gradient(45deg, rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.1), rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.1)),
                  linear-gradient(to bottom, #f0f9ff, #e0f2fe);
      color: #0f172a;
    }

    /* Test 7: Gradient with oklch colors (modern CSS) - SHOULD PASS */
    .test-oklch {
      background: linear-gradient(to right, oklch(0.95 0.02 250), oklch(0.92 0.03 280));
      color: #1e293b;
    }

    /* Test 8: Barely passing gradient contrast - SHOULD be info, not error */
    .test-barely-pass {
      background: linear-gradient(to right, #f8f8f8, #f0f0f0);
      color: #737373;
    }

    /* Test 9: Gradient that makes text invisible - SHOULD FAIL */
    .test-invisible {
      background: linear-gradient(to right, #ef4444, #f97316);
      color: #dc2626;
    }

    /* Test 10: Conic gradient (not supported yet) */
    .test-conic {
      background: conic-gradient(from 0deg, #f8fafc, #e2e8f0, #f8fafc);
      color: #1e293b;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Gradient Contrast Edge Cases</h1>

  <div class="label">Test 1: Multiple linear-gradient layers (white 85% overlay)</div>
  <div class="test-card test-multi-gradient">
    <p>Easily create accurate translations for your content in minutes.</p>
    <div class="expect">Expected: PASS (black on near-white ~18:1). Bug previously reported this as 1.66:1</div>
  </div>

  <div class="label">Test 2: Radial gradient dot pattern</div>
  <div class="test-card test-radial-dot">
    <p>This text sits on a subtle radial dot pattern with a beige background color.</p>
    <div class="expect">Expected: PASS (dark text on beige ~15:1). Radial dots are tiny and shouldn't affect reading</div>
  </div>

  <div class="label">Test 3: Dark diagonal gradient</div>
  <div class="test-card test-dark-gradient">
    <p>Light text on a dark diagonal gradient background.</p>
    <div class="expect">Expected: PASS (light on dark ~11:1)</div>
  </div>

  <div class="label">Test 4: Low contrast gradient (should fail)</div>
  <div class="test-card test-low-contrast">
    <p>Gray text on a light gray gradient — this should be flagged.</p>
    <div class="expect">Expected: FAIL (gray on gray ~1.5-2:1)</div>
  </div>

  <div class="label">Test 5: Semi-transparent overlay on white</div>
  <div class="test-card test-semi-transparent">
    <p>Nearly black text on a barely tinted white surface.</p>
    <div class="expect">Expected: PASS (near-black on near-white ~19:1)</div>
  </div>

  <div class="label">Test 6: Triple-layer gradient stack</div>
  <div class="test-card test-triple-layer">
    <p>Dark text on three stacked gradient layers that composite to near-white.</p>
    <div class="expect">Expected: PASS (dark on composited near-white ~18:1)</div>
  </div>

  <div class="label">Test 7: oklch gradient colors</div>
  <div class="test-card test-oklch">
    <p>Dark text on a subtle oklch gradient background.</p>
    <div class="expect">Expected: PASS (dark on light ~11:1). Tests modern color format support.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="label">Test 8: Barely passing contrast</div>
  <div class="test-card test-barely-pass">
    <p>Medium gray text on a very light gradient.</p>
    <div class="expect">Expected: INFO (barely passes ~4.5-5:1). Should NOT be error or warning.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="label">Test 9: Gradient that hides text (should fail)</div>
  <div class="test-card test-invisible">
    <p>Red text on a red-orange gradient — nearly invisible.</p>
    <div class="expect">Expected: FAIL (red on red ~1.2:1)</div>
  </div>

  <div class="label">Test 10: Conic gradient (fallback)</div>
  <div class="test-card test-conic">
    <p>Text on a conic gradient — parser may not support this yet.</p>
    <div class="expect">Expected: Either PASS or UNCERTAIN (conic not parsed → white fallback → passes)</div>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
