      <h4>Audience Profiles — Evidence-Based Thresholds</h4>
      <p>Each profile adjusts scoring thresholds based on published accessibility research. Switching re-scores instantly.</p>
      <table>
        <tr><th></th><th>Contrast</th><th>Font min</th><th>Touch</th><th>Key change</th></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>General</strong></td><td>4.5:1</td><td>16px</td><td>24/44px</td><td>WCAG AA baseline</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>WCAG AAA</strong></td><td>7:1</td><td>16px</td><td>24/44px</td><td>Enhanced contrast</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Elderly</strong></td><td>7:1</td><td>18px</td><td>48px</td><td>12px spacing, max 7 nav, no thin fonts, reduced motion</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Low Vision</strong></td><td>7:1</td><td>18px</td><td>44px</td><td>12px spacing, 32px icons, bg image warnings</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Motor</strong></td><td>4.5:1</td><td>16px</td><td>48px</td><td>12px spacing, focus indicator checks</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Color Vision</strong></td><td>4.5:1</td><td>16px</td><td>24/44px</td><td>CVD palette simulation, red-green reliance</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Children</strong></td><td>4.5:1</td><td>18px</td><td>48px</td><td>16px spacing, grade 5 reading, max 5 nav</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Cognitive</strong></td><td>4.5:1</td><td>16px</td><td>24/44px</td><td>Grade 8 reading, max 5 nav, reduced motion</td></tr>
      </table>
      <details style="margin-top:10px">
        <summary style="font-size:12px;color:var(--text-secondary);cursor:pointer">Sources</summary>
        <ul style="font-size:11px;color:var(--text-secondary);margin-top:6px;padding-left:18px;line-height:1.6">
          <li><strong>Contrast 4.5:1 / 7:1</strong> — <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/#contrast-minimum" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WCAG 2.2 §1.4.3</a> (AA) and <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/#contrast-enhanced" target="_blank" rel="noopener">§1.4.6</a> (AAA)</li>
          <li><strong>Touch target 44px</strong> — <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/#target-size-minimum" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WCAG 2.2 §2.5.8</a>; 48dp from <a href="https://m3.material.io/foundations/layout/applying-layout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Material Design 3</a></li>
          <li><strong>Click target 24px</strong> — <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/#target-size-minimum" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WCAG 2.2 §2.5.8</a> minimum for non-inline targets</li>
          <li><strong>16px body text</strong> — Browser default; <a href="https://www.nngroup.com/articles/let-users-control-font-size/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NNGroup research</a> on minimum legibility</li>
          <li><strong>18px for elderly</strong> — <a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/older-users/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">W3C WAI Older Users</a> and <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/#dfn-large-scale" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WCAG large text definition</a> (18pt = 24px, 14pt bold = 18.5px)</li>
          <li><strong>48px targets for motor/elderly</strong> — <a href="https://m3.material.io/foundations/layout/applying-layout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Material Design 3</a> (48dp); <a href="https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/accessibility" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apple HIG</a> (44pt)</li>
          <li><strong>12px target spacing</strong> — <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/#target-size-minimum" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WCAG 2.2 §2.5.8</a> spacing exception; Motor impairment research via <a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/GL/task-forces/coga/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">COGA Task Force</a></li>
          <li><strong>Line height 1.4–1.6</strong> — <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/#text-spacing" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WCAG 2.2 §1.4.12</a> (1.5× minimum); <a href="https://practicaltypography.com/line-spacing.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Butterick's Practical Typography</a></li>
          <li><strong>No thin fonts for elderly</strong> — <a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/older-users/developing/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">W3C WAI Developing for Older Users</a>: avoid font-weight below 400</li>
          <li><strong>CVD palette simulation</strong> — <a href="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/~oliveira/pubs_files/CVD_Simulation/CVD_Simulation.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Machado et al. 2009</a>; <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/#use-of-color" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WCAG 2.2 §1.4.1</a></li>
          <li><strong>Reading level Grade 5/8</strong> — <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/#reading-level" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WCAG 2.2 §3.1.5</a>; Flesch-Kincaid / Coleman-Liau index</li>
          <li><strong>Max 5 nav items</strong> — <a href="https://doi.org/10.1017/S0140525X01003922" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cowan (2001)</a>: working memory 4±1; <a href="https://www.nngroup.com/articles/childrens-websites-usability-issues/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NNGroup children UX</a></li>
          <li><strong>Children touch targets</strong> — <a href="https://www.nngroup.com/articles/children-ux-physical-development/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NNGroup Physical Development</a>: 48px min, 76px ideal for ages 4-8</li>
          <li><strong>Cognitive/COGA</strong> — <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/coga-usable/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">W3C Making Content Usable</a>: short sentences, consistent nav, icon+text</li>
        </ul>
      </details>
